          <p>
            <strong>For a shake that tastes like a treat:</strong> vanilla or one of the non-cocoa flavors in the standard stevia version, which keeps added sugar at zero. If you dislike stevia, the stevia-free versions trade it for monk fruit and about 4 g of coconut sugar. Keep cocoa-based flavors such as chocolate, mocha and chocolate mint for a few times a week.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>For on-the-go protein:</strong> the Prime Bar gives about 20 g of beef protein in a bar sweetened with dates and honey. It is a whole-food style bar, so expect more calories and sugar than a shake; it suits hikes, travel and busy days better than cutting. <strong>For carnivore or paleo diets:</strong> unflavored, mixed with water, coffee or bone broth.
          </p>

          <p>
            Whatever you choose, use it to fill gaps rather than replace meals. Real beef, eggs and fish give you the same amino acids with more nutrients per dollar. If you are still deciding between beef powders, our <a href="/best-beef-protein-powder/">best beef protein powder</a> ranking compares Equip with Transparent Labs, Carnivor and others on dose, testing and cost.
          </p>
